# ART-58: A cold start clears the whole print staging directory.
#
# App.onCreate calls PrintController.sweepStaging exactly once per process, and
# instrumentation shares the app process, so the sweep a test wants to observe
# has already run before its first line. The only honest way to see it run again
# is a host driven kill between two instrumentation invocations, which is what
# the artifacts spec anticipated when it flagged this test as possibly needing
# the phase runner.
#
# No launch-view and no launch-task. Nothing needs to be on screen: starting the
# instrumentation for phase two is itself what creates the application object
# and runs its onCreate, and that is the whole subject of the test.
#
# clearPackageData is off after phase one, so the cache directory phase one
# wrote survives the kill. That is the channel under test.
describe A cold start clears the whole print staging directory

# Writes three files into cacheDir/print, one of them a whole copy of
# small-300kb.pdf, and one quote card into cacheDir/share.
phase com.gitlab.mudlej.MjPdfReader.suite.artifacts.PrintStagingColdStartTest#phaseOneStageThreeFilesForPrintAndOneForSharing

kill-app

# Asserts cacheDir/print is empty and cacheDir/share is untouched, since the
# share cache has its own age based policy and no cold start rule.
phase com.gitlab.mudlej.MjPdfReader.suite.artifacts.PrintStagingColdStartTest#phaseTwoAssertTheColdStartClearedPrintStagingAndLeftTheShareCache
